{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>May YHWH make His face shine upon you.</b> Like the sense of 'the brightening of a king's face is life,' and the meaning is: whatever you ask of Him — and when you seek Him, He will brighten His face, and the meaning is He will receive you and be willing to fulfill your request immediately." "And if you seek Him in a time of trouble, He <b>will be gracious to you.</b> It is also possible that 'and He will be gracious to you' means 'and He will grant your request,' like the sense of 'show me grace, you whom Elohim has graced' — from the root חנן."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "Resolved מלא' as מלאות (fulfillment); the apostrophe abbreviates a final letter."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:16:39.252981488Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}